   ]
  },
  "sentences": [
   {
    "role": "hook",
    "text": "If you stand uranium rods in a tank of water, you have a reactor."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem",
    "text": "But the water boils, and the steam escapes."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix1",
    "text": "So you pipe the steam to a turbine that spins a generator."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem2",
    "text": "But now the reaction speeds up, and the rods glow red."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix2",
    "text": "So you lower control rods that soak up neutrons."
   },
   {
    "role": "name",
    "text": "This is a nuclear power plant."
   },
   {
    "role": "how",
    "text": "Steam spins the turbine, and power runs along the lines."
   },
   {
    "role": "problem3",
    "text": "But now steam piles up, and the turbine stalls."
   },
   {
    "role": "fix3",
    "text": "So a cooling tower cools the steam; its white cloud is water vapor."
   },
   {
    "role": "fact",
    "text": "One fuel pellet makes about as much energy as one ton of coal."
   },
   {
    "role": "finish",
    "text": "Add a concrete dome over the reactor."
   },
   {
    "role": "congrats",
    "text": "Congratulations, you have built a nuclear power plant."
   }
